{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1478208-dragon-blooded-descended-from-first-age-loyalists","id":1478208,"title":"Dragon-Blooded descended from First Age loyalists?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Dragon-Blooded"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-04-07T07:39:20-07:00","id":1478208,"title":"Dragon-Blooded descended from First Age loyalists?","content":"I've started on the Dragon-Blooded books, and a thought suddenly popped up, one that for some reason never occurred to me before: What if, somewhere in Creation, there existed a Dragon-Blooded culture descended from those Terrestrials who fought to defend the Solars during the Usurpation? What if some survived and fled to the edges of the world alongside the Lunars, disgusted by the usurpers? What would they look like? What would they become, unaffected by the lies of the Immaculate Philosophy? What stories would they tell their children, of a paradise lost to treachery and base usurpers, usurpers who justify their rule with lies about the nature of Heaven, the Elemental Dragons and reincarnation? How they and they alone are the only Terrestrials who do not carry traitor's blood in their veins?<br /> After a thousand years they, like the Lunars, wouldn't be expecting the return of the Solars. They would have their own plans and dreams. But then the leader of the heretics and traitors disappears during Calibration, and people with the mark of the Unconquered Sun on their brow start appearing in unprecedented numbers.<br /> No doubt many Elders would be disquieted, worried about ancient legends made real. But what would the young and brash think? I wouldn't be surprised if a number of romantics were to think &quot;We will not fail again,&quot; grasp their daiklaves and set out into the world to see if these returned Solars are worthy of their assistance, and if so, to aid in killing the Immaculate filth hunting them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1631-karthak","name":"Karthak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1631_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-16T11:23:15-08:00","id":1500518,"title":"","content":"This group seems less likely to be a healthy remnant of First Age Dragon-Blooded culture and more multi-generational murder cult that's neck deep in its own propaganda. <br /> <br /> For perspective, imagine if the current timeline advanced a thousand years where people aren't sure if the Scarlet Empress was a real person or an allegorical figure but House Iselsi was still enacting the vendetta on the descendants of the other Great Houses.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-17T14:38:21-08:00","id":1500528,"title":"","content":"This feels like a very 2e take on a dragonblooded culture.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/8fsIR2T.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13566-kalzky","name":"Kalzky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13566_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-18T05:09:27-08:00","id":1500598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kalzky</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1478208-dragon-blooded-descended-from-first-age-loyalists?p=1500528#post1500528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This feels like a very 2e take on a dragonblooded culture.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a rhetoric that elevates it above the more reasonable desire for a group of Dragon-Blooded who don't mind working for/with you.<br /> <br /> I've honestly missed this kind of thing in the years this forum has been too broken to function.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 01-18-2023, 08:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-18T06:12:12-08:00","id":1500603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karthak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1478208-dragon-blooded-descended-from-first-age-loyalists#post1478208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've started on the Dragon-Blooded books, and a thought suddenly popped up, one that for some reason never occurred to me before: What if, somewhere in Creation, there existed a Dragon-Blooded culture descended from those Terrestrials who fought to defend the Solars during the Usurpation? What if some survived and fled to the edges of the world alongside the Lunars, disgusted by the usurpers? What would they look like? What would they become, unaffected by the lies of the Immaculate Philosophy? What stories would they tell their children, of a paradise lost to treachery and base usurpers, usurpers who justify their rule with lies about the nature of Heaven, the Elemental Dragons and reincarnation? How they and they alone are the only Terrestrials who do not carry traitor's blood in their veins?<br /> After a thousand years they, like the Lunars, wouldn't be expecting the return of the Solars. They would have their own plans and dreams. But then the leader of the heretics and traitors disappears during Calibration, and people with the mark of the Unconquered Sun on their brow start appearing in unprecedented numbers.<br /> No doubt many Elders would be disquieted, worried about ancient legends made real. But what would the young and brash think? I wouldn't be surprised if a number of romantics were to think &quot;We will not fail again,&quot; grasp their daiklaves and set out into the world to see if these returned Solars are worthy of their assistance, and if so, to aid in killing the Immaculate filth hunting them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Without getting too contemporary, the Solar Purge was something like 1500 years ago.<br /> <br /> It's like saying, what if there was an enclave of Germans who fought against the Visigoths in the Fall of Rome.<br /> <br /> For the most part, survivors of each side have interbred, moved on, consigned it to the history books.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying it couldn't happen, just that it's probably not as interesting and polarized as it might first appear.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-18T07:44:28-08:00","id":1500607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karthak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1478208-dragon-blooded-descended-from-first-age-loyalists#post1478208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've started on the Dragon-Blooded books, and a thought suddenly popped up, one that for some reason never occurred to me before: What if, somewhere in Creation, there existed a Dragon-Blooded culture descended from those Terrestrials who fought to defend the Solars during the Usurpation? What if some survived and fled to the edges of the world alongside the Lunars, disgusted by the usurpers? What would they look like? What would they become, unaffected by the lies of the Immaculate Philosophy? What stories would they tell their children, of a paradise lost to treachery and base usurpers, usurpers who justify their rule with lies about the nature of Heaven, the Elemental Dragons and reincarnation? How they and they alone are the only Terrestrials who do not carry traitor's blood in their veins?<br /> After a thousand years they, like the Lunars, wouldn't be expecting the return of the Solars. They would have their own plans and dreams. But then the leader of the heretics and traitors disappears during Calibration, and people with the mark of the Unconquered Sun on their brow start appearing in unprecedented numbers.<br /> No doubt many Elders would be disquieted, worried about ancient legends made real. But what would the young and brash think? I wouldn't be surprised if a number of romantics were to think &quot;We will not fail again,&quot; grasp their daiklaves and set out into the world to see if these returned Solars are worthy of their assistance, and if so, to aid in killing the Immaculate filth hunting them.</div> </div> </div> </div>An alternative tract here, but if you wanted to skirt the time gap you could have it that their civilisation has been locked outside of time since during the Usurpation up until recently, 'recently' being however long you personally think it to be feasible.<br /> <br /> Why were they locked outside of time? Was it inflicted on them? A defence against overwhelming odds? A secret contingency?<br /> <br /> Something similar is happening in our game right now and it's a blast. A vast city fortress just showed up between Paragon and Chiaroscuro after we tried punch away a major gnarl of destiny. It's loaded with weaponry, automata with Solar Hungry Ghosts and Dragonblooded elites who made a sworn oath to preserve the freedom and mythical privileges they had under the Solar patrons of their former kingdom. This is during a major clusterfuck Blessed Isle Civil War as well, and we're the poor Bronze Faction guys that have to deal with it and talk them out of their principles, which is something we're still delving into and can't snappily be summed up in a post like this.<br /> <br /> This is obviously crazy, dramatic and certainly not as subtle or nearly as historically continuous as your suggestion. Maybe offering a very extreme view might inspire you though","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26024-distant-choir","name":"Distant Choir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26024_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-18T18:10:54-08:00","id":1500685,"title":"","content":"In my setting headcanon, during the Shogunate there were Dragon Blooded gens that retained their loyalty to the Solar Exalted. They did so secretly, of course. And there were a couple of instances of that Solar being reborn, their Dragon Blooded loyalists coming to collect them, and then eventually that clan of Dragon Blooded being hunted down and fighting to the death. These handful of instances, in turn, caused the Immaculate Order of the time period to create an inquisition to investigate Dragon Blood gens searching for loyalty to the Solar Exalted. <br /> <br /> By the time of the Great Contagion pretty much none of the surviving Dragon Blooded gens still retained any loyalty to the Solar Exalted. By that time those had had been loyal had had that loyalty uncovered and they'd been killed, or they had thrown their lot in with one of the reborn Solar Exalted and been destroyed. By the modern time period, there aren't any left. It's possible that some Dragon Blooded families in the Threshold might have some ancient ties, and maybe a Dragon Blooded could find some long-forgotten secret library in their family manse and it would reveal that at one time, their ancestors had been Solar loyalists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-19T01:38:09-08:00","id":1500707,"title":"","content":"I'd imagine the early Shogunate was full of Dragon-Blooded who had no idea the Usurpation was going to happen and resented being dragged kicking and screaming into a new era, but didn't have anyone to rally behind. In-part because they were more likely to be loyal to specific individuals than the Solar Exalts as a whole. Those who liked the Solar Deliberative and saw it as a stable one world government probably had more reason to try and make the Shogunate work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-19T12:08:51-08:00","id":1500755,"title":"","content":"One thing that occurred to me was some gens of Dragonblooded given some task by a First Age Solar (especially as the Sidereals 3rd Ed book makes the Usurpation messy, enough to make it possible a Solar knew something was up, but not what) and that is the focus of this small Outcaste community. Like 'here is my research/neat artifacts/manse/McGuffin/etc., you lot guard it for me until I get back', and the elders decided when 'all of the Solars are dead and the Lunars have all gotten out of dodge', that meant 'guard the McGuffin until our Solar's next incarnation shows up, since htey don't take that long to incarnate normally'. While 1500 years is a lot of time, Dragonblooded folks also live several times longer than baseline humans, so it might be more like 'great-great-grandpa's stories about the US Civil War that are family legends' than 'Visigoths' scale, and having a tangible thing gives a focus especially with Creation having plenty of beings who would love to steal a First Age Solar's stuff in a place other than a fancy trapped tomb built to appease a First Age Solar's ghost by keeping their grave goods safe.<br /> <br /> It also makes it personal having an actual historical figure or figures (a Circle, for instance), with the abstract question about the Usurpation being framed around 'the other Exalted that betrayed great-great-granddad's lord were assholes, but we are the last remnants of honor among the Dragonbloods', and maybe largely an abstract question... until the Solars come back, and are looking for answers, and suddenly they might have to hand the McGuffin over to the next incarnation of its owner's Shard.<br /> <br /> One could also play with how much actually was known (and how much was known but wrong) because it is essentially family legend and its own sort of religious belief. Maybe the family isn't really sure it was a Solar versus something else from well before the Contagion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24133-stareyes","name":"Stareyes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-21T02:04:19-08:00","id":1500911,"title":"","content":"I think your most effective way to do this kind of thing is to have a culture that comes across as though it <i>originates</i> as distinctly against the Solar Purge, and in its modern time has evolved into something that in practical terms is more about having a historical and ideological opposition to the manner of Dragon Blooded rule and conduct found in the Shogunate and its successors. In practical terms I think that means their society functions differently, and it would probably generate the most history and drama if they were close enough to at least one of the other Dragon Blooded powers for there to have been some wars in their time.<br /> <br /> For all the talk of the first post being very Second Edition, I feel as though the suggestions of a Shogunate gens that retains loyalty to a surviving Solar to the point of fighting the world for them is also very much arising from an assumption of complete subservience that was more native to that Edition than this one. First Age Dragon Blooded with something like that relationship to a Solar make sense, but I feel as though the Shogunate would have put them in the position of needing to make some very difficult choices rather than just being totally on board with fighting a losing battle down to the last body out of principle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-21T14:10:54-08:00","id":1500961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1478208-dragon-blooded-descended-from-first-age-loyalists?p=1500911#post1500911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For all the talk of the first post being very Second Edition, I feel as though the suggestions of a Shogunate gens that retains loyalty to a surviving Solar to the point of fighting the world for them is also very much arising from an assumption of complete subservience that was more native to that Edition than this one. First Age Dragon Blooded with something like that relationship to a Solar make sense, but I feel as though the Shogunate would have put them in the position of needing to make some very difficult choices rather than just being totally on board with fighting a losing battle down to the last body out of principle.</div> </div> </div> </div>AnubisXy's post? My reading of it was more that if their sympathies for the old establishment were discovered their only real option was to go down swinging. Which is still pretty 2e but in a different way. <br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-22T18:59:23-08:00","id":1501088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1478208-dragon-blooded-descended-from-first-age-loyalists?p=1500961#post1500961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">AnubisXy's post? My reading of it was more that if their sympathies for the old establishment were discovered their only real option was to go down swinging. Which is still pretty 2e but in a different way.<br /> <br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>That was more or less my idea, yeah. There were probably some Gens that had never really hated the Solar Exalted and were blindsided by the Shogunate rebellion. By the time they knew what was happening, it was basically over and too late. Most of those Gens transitioned to the new system because they didn't have much of a choice. It's likely that at least a few made some cursory moves towards supporting the Shogunate, but still secretly retained some level of loyalty to the old Deliberative. Most likely those were Gens that found themselves on the bottom end of the new political system and looked back with rose-tinted glasses at the previous system, or imagined a newer system where they would have more power. In the event that their disloyalty to the Shogunate was discovered, they'd risk being put to the sword.<br /> <br /> Keep in mind that there were lots of rebellions and warfare in the Shogunate as various Gens battled and fought one another for power. Some of those rebellious Gens may have ended up with Solar figureheads and/or allies (or possibly Lunar ones too). And I'd expect that there would end up being some sort of Inquisition-type organization devoted to not just hunting down reborn Solar Exalted but also exposing those Gens who didn't display appropriate loyalty to the new Shogunate, and that also didn't accept the historical revisions that were being created and spread (Solars being puppets of the Yozi and such).<br /> <br /> Over time any Gens that retained some level of loyalty to the old system ended up becoming something like &quot;crypto-Jews&quot; with families concealing their beliefs in the form of artwork, architecture or stories in order to hide from an Inquisition that was looking to exterminate them. Some of those things might have survived the Contagion and Wyld invasion and can be found in the modern world, though by this point only the greatest of scholars could recognize some of those traditions or displays for what they originally meant.<br /> <br /> So by the current era, these end up being little more than a historical quirk, and none of the descendants from those families have any sort of loyalty to Solar Exalted, just some slightly unusual family traditions. Still, it could be part of a Dragon Blooded PC's background, and during the course of a campaign they could uncover the past about their family or something like that, but this would be a sort of one-off event and not something you'd see on any sort of major scale.<br /> <br /> *edit* Just to reiterate, these sorts of families would be very much exceptional. The vast majority of Dragon Blooded, even those that had generally been more supportive of the Solar Deliberative would have dropped their loyalty when it became apparent that the Solars were not coming back en masse. After a few decades they would have said, &quot;Well, I guess it really is a new world and a new order and it's time to get in on that.&quot; Still, there likely were some Gens, or parts of some Gens, that preferred the old system to the new one for various reasons and would have needed to take steps to hide that fact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 01-22-2023, 11:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-03T20:32:46-08:00","id":1502079,"title":"","content":"I feel like any such organization would probably be pretty cult like and heavily indoctrinate its members if it has managed to keep an ongoing bloodline of dragon blooded that is still mad about the usurpation 1500 years later. Assuming an average generation is about 30 years or so that puts it at having to keep roughly 50 generations of dragon blooded on the same track devoted to a cause that is increasingly farther back into the fog of history. It seems way more likely that, instead of some family still pissed about the usurpation in particular, that you have a family that has been attached to some lunar elder or another as a family friend and patron for that time period and their loyalty is to them as opposed to some long dead government. Sure they will humor the guy and agree that it totally sucked if the Lunar elder brings it up but the dragon blooded clan isn't likely to actually feel particularly strongly about it compared to focusing on more recent injuries inflicted by the realm and sidereal within living memory of their clan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-07T11:57:24-08:00","id":1502406,"title":"","content":"I think there is some in Luthe? I'd have to double check <i>Fangs at the Gate</i> though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-08T05:55:16-08:00","id":1502504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1478208-dragon-blooded-descended-from-first-age-loyalists?p=1502406#post1502406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think there is some in Luthe? I'd have to double check <i>Fangs at the Gate</i> though.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's one named Dragon-Blooded NPC but he differs from what the OP was asking for in a couple of important ways, he's never even heard of the Usurpation and comes across more as an unaligned outcaste who has Leviathan as one of his clients.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-09T06:03:58-08:00","id":1502600,"title":"","content":"True but it does imply they do exist there","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-11T18:21:43-08:00","id":1502800,"title":"","content":"He is a dragon blooded who works with a lunar but otherwise they don't really meet the criteria for TCs idea of an entire clan of dragon blooded who make a big deal out of still being loyal to the solar deliberative 1500 years later and despising the usurpers that overthrew them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-07T15:25:26-08:00","id":1528180,"title":"","content":"1. You'd need to be far, far the fuck away from the Blessed Isle, natch.<br /> 2. Your ancestors need a hell of a story as to why they were left breathing by the Sidereals, who would have several vested interests in killing them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-12T17:39:37-08:00","id":1545758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kalzky</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1478208-dragon-blooded-descended-from-first-age-loyalists?p=1500528#post1500528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This feels like a very 2e take on a dragonblooded culture.</div> </div> </div> </div>With the removal of dynasty charms the potential for such things does not exist in 3rd edition<br /> <br /> <br /> just curious if a solar wanted a dragon blooded servant odds are good the dragon blooded has at least one opposing intimacy","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-21T12:17:02-07:00","id":1551807,"title":"","content":"One thought I have on this subject, is in a DB blooded game it could be a point of embarrassment or a Mystery Investigation... Given how much longer Terrestrials live for, or the uncovering of Gene-Locked Artifacts, that they are descended from ancestors who were quiet solar sympathizers for a few generations before forgetting about it. (Likely during the many wars of the Shogunate or the Great Contagion.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-15T09:31:32-07:00","id":1552417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tytalus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1478208-dragon-blooded-descended-from-first-age-loyalists?p=1551807#post1551807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thought I have on this subject, is in a DB blooded game it could be a point of embarrassment or a Mystery Investigation... Given how much longer Terrestrials live for, or the uncovering of Gene-Locked Artifacts, that they are descended from ancestors who were quiet solar sympathizers for a few generations before forgetting about it. (Likely during the many wars of the Shogunate or the Great Contagion.)</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, i'd imagine any large group of Terrestrials that felt strongly about the Usurpation for either personal or romantic/historic revisionist reasons would have transfered their loyalties to a Lunar survivor or other sufficiently charismatic-puisant claimant to the Deliberative by sometime in the mid-Shogunate (that stood for more than 7 centuries - and who knows how much longer it might have endured if not for the Contagion-Fae Onslaight combo).<br /> <br /> What only brings home my feeling that we need more materials exploring the Shogunate as an actual era with nations, cultures and centuries of history of its own instead of a &quot;skip button era&quot;/speed bump between Usurpation and Contagion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-15T11:58:24-07:00","id":1552421,"title":"","content":"As an aside, does anyone remember something about a Cadet House in the South that is not only older than the Realm, but probably the Shogunate (if not pre-Solar Deliberative)?<br /> I'm pretty sure i read it somewhere but can't remember if it was WFHW, Heirs of the Shogunate, the Realm or somewhere else altogether.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-15T22:00:43-07:00","id":1552440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1478208-dragon-blooded-descended-from-first-age-loyalists?p=1552421#post1552421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As an aside, does anyone remember something about a Cadet House in the South that is not only older than the Realm, but probably the Shogunate (if not pre-Solar Deliberative)?<br /> I'm pretty sure i read it somewhere but can't remember if it was WFHW, Heirs of the Shogunate, the Realm or somewhere else altogether.</div> </div> </div> </div>You'd have to just CTRL-F the pdf file to find it, I can't recall either. 3e is much better about expanding the DB houses scattered around.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-16T02:03:38-07:00","id":1552442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tytalus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1478208-dragon-blooded-descended-from-first-age-loyalists?p=1552440#post1552440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You'd have to just CTRL-F the pdf file to find it, I can't recall either. 3e is much better about expanding the DB houses scattered around.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Time to dive back into the books for that juicy lore kernels then. Even if i find nothing i already have the seed of a bad, mad idea to toy with, i guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 07-16-2025, 05:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-16T20:25:04-07:00","id":1552472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1478208-dragon-blooded-descended-from-first-age-loyalists?p=1552442#post1552442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Time to dive back into the books for that juicy lore kernels then. Even if i find nothing i already have the seed of a bad, mad idea to toy with, i guess.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tell me more. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-21T07:08:51-07:00","id":1552558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tytalus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1478208-dragon-blooded-descended-from-first-age-loyalists?p=1552472#post1552472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Tell me more. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Found it, House Simendor, in pages 17-20 of Heirs to the Shogunate. The house founder was Simendor the Hellblade, a dragon-blooded daimyo that, among other things served as an early tutor on sorcerous arts to the Empress herself and whose ancestors were sorcerer-princes who sat the Agate Throne of Chalan since the long-forgotten First Age, enduring under many names and banners since.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heirs to the Shogunate, pg.18</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>In a time now lost to history, House Simendor\u2019s ancestors cavorted with spirits of sand and shadow in the open desert \u2014 <b>rogue gods and elementals who refused to bow to the Old Realm. </b>Fromthis so-called<b> Court of Nameless Gods</b>, they learned the art of sorcery. Today, many scions still honor their house\u2019s traditions by initiating into sorcery under these spirits\u2019 tutelage, seeking out their hidden pleasure-sanctums.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>A little nice citation just to set a bit of a tone for things. No straight out assertion of the house's precise antiquity, but evocative enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 07-21-2025, 01:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-25T13:32:38-08:00","id":1555864,"title":"","content":"Just to throw my own 2\u00a2 into this old well, I think it depends on what counts as &quot;loyalty.&quot;<br /> <br /> Because as many others have said, it's sorta nonsense to define yourself <i>as a political entity</i> by schisms that are ancient history and that you don't have any actionable means to engage with. But I don't actually think that's the main lens to look at this through.<br /> <br /> The thought first occurred to me with Lookshy and their concept of the True Heir to the Shogunate (TM), actually, but applies equally well here. A story about &quot;an ancient leader of a golden age whose death precipitated the current age of garbage but who will come back and lead us to a new golden age some day if we maintain devotion through generations of hardship&quot; isn't really a political policy - it's a <i>religion</i>. Not the normative model of a religion in Creation, where most divinities are very active and reinforce their own worship, I'll grant, but an archetypal one for humanity, which I've gotta assume people in Creation are similar enough to real humans to come up with. Especially in a setting where the things that could facilitate such great figures returning - reincarnation (both of the human soul and Exaltation), ancient ghosts, tremendous lifespans and places/magics that can stretch those further, hereditary supernatural power, etc - are just as concretely real as all those divinities.<br /> <br /> Now, religions undergo tons of permutation over time and are often founded in the first place on propaganda, so they're not gonna have, like, an <i>accurate</i> view of the First Age, or the Shogunate, or whatnot. And the point that people's <i>politics</i> will focus on their present daily concerns remains salient. To the extent that anybody will know or care about ancient schisms, it'll be to the forms and extents that Christians a thousand+ years removed from ancient Rome know or care about ancient Rome - pretty jerk move to kill Jesus; the feeding Christians to lions thing makes a good allegory to whatever sense of persecution and hardship you're perceiving in the present world; maybe a few nebulously-historical mental images of their fashion and cultural mores invoked by storytellers; but that's sorta it. They're long gone, only the nerds with too much free time care what they thought about anything else. The main utility of any bits and pieces of oral history that remain prevalent about those ancient days will be as a shared cultural lens for interpreting and responding to current events the group is dealing with.<br /> <br /> Also important: religions syncretize as much as they permute internally, and 1500+ years is an entire immense history for this religion in its own right, so if they're close enough to Immaculacy to have cultural exchange with them, you could easily expect them to nudge their mental model of their savior so it doesn't overlap with those terrible Anathema. Being founded on loyalty to Solars <i>could</i> mean seeing Solars as your ancient heroes reborn today, but that's far from a guarantee. Hell, they could've had a schism about that 600 years ago, and one group gets driven out and goes to preach someplace and then the original group falls apart for some reason and now the main adherents of the descended-from-loyalists religion aren't even descended from the loyalists anymore.<br /> <br /> It's a long time; stuff happens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28948-mj6373","name":"MJ6373","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}